  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>At the entrance to Saint-Tropez, on the edge of Gassin, La Bouillabaisse is a wide white-sand beach facing the Maures massif, shared between private establishments (beach restaurants) and public shoreline. The tourist office presents it as the best spot to watch the sun set behind the Maures. The conceded section runs from the boundary with Gassin to a wooden footbridge to the east (town of Saint-Tropez).</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>On the beaches of the town of Saint-Tropez, municipal bylaw no. 1828/2026 of 6 July 2026 allows dogs on the town's beaches from 6am to 9:30am and from 6:30pm to 10pm, from 16 July to 15 September 2026; outside those time slots, they are banned. Dogs must remain under their owner's constant responsibility and be kept on a leash when other users are nearby and whenever circumstances require; the bylaw does not apply to walkers with dogs on a leash on the coastal path. It only covers that period: for the rest of the year, no published rule was found, so rely on the signs on site. The Saint-Tropez Tourisme tourist office page for this beach, however, says "Dogs are banned", with no reference to these hours — probably a page not updated since the bylaw, but this is not guaranteed. Check the signs on site before settling in with your dog.</p>
      <p>Bylaw no. 1828/2026, signed on 6 July 2026 and published on 21 July 2026, also sets the owner's duties: pick up droppings immediately, ensure public tranquillity, not damage facilities or natural areas, and respect other users as well as the fauna and flora. Guide dogs, assistance dogs and those of the rescue or police services are excluded from the time-based ban. The 2026 period ended on 15 September; the rule in force in 2027 is not known to date.</p>
      <p>The tourist office page describes the beach as a wide stretch of white sand facing the Maures massif, between beach restaurants and public shoreline, with a lifeguard post in season, toilets, nearby parking and wheelchair access with assistance. Access is free all year. According to the town of Saint-Tropez, the concession covers 8,805 m² with 310 m of beach frontage, and the conceded section runs from the boundary with Gassin to a wooden footbridge to the east.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the Gassin-side part depends on that town's rules, not Saint-Tropez's — and the 2025 "Dog friendly" leaflet of the Ramatuelle tourist office states that, in Gassin, dogs are only allowed on certain beaches (<a href="/en/fiche-plage-moune-gassin">La Moune</a> and <a href="/en/fiche-plage-treizain-gassin">Le Treizain</a>). Stay on the Saint-Tropez side with your dog.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The historic centre of Saint-Tropez is just past the town entrance. For another walk on the gulf side, see the <a href="/fiche-balade-sentier-littoral-grimaud">Port Grimaud coastal path</a>.</p>
